  "query_preview": "..\nIsolated showers and thunderstorms are expected tonight and tomorrow\nmorning for Guam and Rota with shower coverage becoming scattered \nover Tinian and Saipan. Shower coverage will become scattered for all\nislands by tomorrow afternoon as light and variable winds allow \nisland effect showers to develop over at least Guam and Rota. Monday \nnight through Wednesday, dry weather will persist with very gradually\nincreasing westerlies pushing any island effect showers offshore. By\nWednesday night, a developing tropical disturbance to the northeast \nwill bring increased moisture into the Marianas with breezy \nconditions developing Thursday night or Friday. This disturbance will\nbe monitored closely for potential impacts to the Marianas. Models \ncurrently indicate it drifting north of the Marianas with a monsoon \ntail bringing potentially heavy precipitation, particularily to \nTinian and Saipan. However, high uncertainty remains whether the \nstrongest part of the monsoon tail sits over the Marianas or over the\nfar northern CNMI. A hydrologic outlook may be necessary in the \ncoming days depending on the track and intensity of this disturbance.",
